      "beat": "hook",
      "text": "One grain of wheat, doubled sixty three times.",
      "start": 0.4,
      "end": 3.2
    },
    {
      "beat": "setup",
      "text": "A king offered an inventor any reward he wanted. He asked for wheat on a chessboard.",
      "start": 3.6,
      "end": 10.0
    },
    {
      "beat": "setup",
      "text": "One grain on the first square. Two on the next. Then four, then eight.",
      "start": 10.4,
      "end": 15.8
    },
    {
      "beat": "quiz",
      "text": "Pause. How much wheat is that?",
      "start": 16.2,
      "end": 18.6
    },
    {
      "beat": "reveal",
      "text": "Halfway across the board, four billion grains. A couple hundred tonnes. Easy.",
      "start": 19.0,
      "end": 23.6
    },
    {
      "beat": "reveal",
      "text": "But the full board needs eighteen quintillion grains.",
      "start": 24.0,
      "end": 27.2
    },
    {
      "beat": "twist",
      "text": "That's more wheat than the whole world grows in a thousand years.",
      "start": 27.6,
      "end": 32.2
    },
    {
      "beat": "twist",
      "text": "And the last square alone holds more than all the others combined.",
      "start": 32.6,
      "end": 37.2
    },
    {
      "beat": "loop",
      "text": "One grain. Sixty three doublings.",
      "start": 37.6,
      "end": 39.6
    }
  ],
